# Downstream ownership

Use the contract of the service that owns the field. For example, a catalog owns item details and an audit service owns the item’s activity history. Inject the corresponding generated client at each resolver.

```csharp
var history = await auditClient.GetItemHistoryAsync(
    new GetItemHistoryRequest { ItemId = itemId },
    cancellationToken: cancellationToken);
```

Replace the client, request and identifier with the owning service’s contract. Apply the caller’s permissions when exposing its response.
